# digits32 - the big clock face.
#
# 20x32 with 4px stems, for a 128x128 four-panel build where digits16 looks
# lost. "09:41" comes to 104px, which fits a 128px column with room to spare.
#
# Drawn natively at this size rather than scaled up from digits16. The engine
# already replicates whole pixels through "scale", so a 2x copy of digits16
# would add nothing: what a native drawing buys is finer detail than doubling
# can give, mainly diagonals that step by one pixel instead of two.
#
# Codepoints 45-58 only, matching digits16: - . / then 0-9 then the colon. The
# range has to stay contiguous for glyph indexing, so use a body font for
# labels.
#
# Written in the block form fontgen accepts for tall glyphs, since the
# single-line form would put 670 characters on one line and stop being the
# picture it is meant to be.

@name     digits32
@height   32
@baseline 32
@gap      4


